{
  "additional_concerns": [
    "The representation accepts exposure and designation judgments as inputs. It does not establish their evidential validity or implement the SFC’s holistic assessment; Boolean correspondence cannot validate those upstream judgments.",
    "The source supplies no measurement date, look-through, valuation, netting, aggregation or classification-persistence convention. 'Operative' designation is a sensible temporal input requirement, but its assessment requires evidence not supplied here.",
    "The unrestricted designation disjunct does not change the classification outcome above 50%, because the threshold independently suffices. It should not be read as establishing the scope of the SFC’s discretionary power beyond the footnote-linked below-threshold assessment.",
    "Global conflict blocking can prevent a result even when an independently established route suffices. This is a declared evidential execution policy, not a restriction imposed by the circular.",
    "The three unbound dependency IDs have no supplied descriptions linking them to particular authorities. No catalogue mapping can be established from this packet.",
    "FALSE establishes only absence of the two retained routes on the stated assessment basis. OUT_OF_SCOPE establishes only exclusion from this circular; neither establishes non-complex status under other regimes."
  ],
